.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt SPINANDCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm spinandctl
.Nd read identification and status from SPI NAND
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl d Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
configures chip select zero for SPI mode 0 at 1 MHz, then issues only the
SPI NAND READ ID (0x9f, one dummy byte) and GET FEATURE status (0x0f, feature
address 0xc0) commands.
It prints the returned manufacturer ID, device ID, and status register.
.Pp
It does not issue page read, write enable, program, erase, or feature-write
commands.
.Pp
The device must be a raw SPI character device whose chip select is connected
to the NAND device.
.Pp
This utility reports transport-level identification and status only.
It does not provide NAND data access, ECC, bad-block management, or a
filesystem.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d Ar device
Select the SPI character device.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr spi 4
